{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>You shall not covet silver and gold that is on them</b> — the word <b>אֲשֶׁר</b> (that) is missing; it should read: you shall not covet the silver and gold <b>אֲשֶׁר</b> (that) is on them, that is, their adornment. First He commanded to burn the idolatry itself, which is <b>the carved images of their gods</b>, and He also forbade the ornaments that are upon them, and He further warned: <b>nor shall you bring an abomination into your house, lest you become banned like it</b>, to forbid deriving benefit from all aspects of idolatry — it itself, its appurtenances, its offerings, and its ornaments."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:42.308313742Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}